---
title: App Setup
---

Prepare NAHPU before fieldwork so the app reflects your team's protocols and every device is ready to record data offline.

## Configure the app

- Customize the controlled vocabularies for specimen fields, collection methods, preparation types, and personnel.
- Create useful presets for repeated cataloging workflows and review them with the whole team.
- Confirm the main taxon, field-ID mode, eligible Cataloger, controlled
  vocabularies, and export presets in the [Settings guide](../../usages/settings).
- Install NAHPU from the [Installation guide](../../installation), then update it before departure while you still have reliable internet access.
- Open the app after updating and confirm that projects, settings, and permissions are available.

## Prepare a project

Create a project with a short, descriptive name and review the optional device
setup in the wizard. Confirm the dates, taxonomy readiness, field-ID convention,
and site-identifier convention before collecting begins. The [Projects guide](../../usages/projects)
describes project creation and dashboard operations in detail.

## Run a mock catalog session

Use a real or representative specimen to rehearse the complete workflow: create a record, enter required values, generate a site coordinate when appropriate, attach media, save the record, and review it from the project dashboard. Repeat the exercise on every field device and resolve differences before departure.

## Confirm field readiness

Before leaving, confirm that each device has enough storage, a charged battery and backup power, the latest NAHPU version, the correct project, and the required location and camera permissions. Test airplane-mode operation if the field site may lack connectivity. Then rehearse both recovery paths once: export the project and merge it back on a second device, and make one database backup that can be restored.
